# Battlezone Auxiliary PCB 035678-01 -- netlist, read by eye
#
# Source: DP-156 sheet 3 Side B, 2nd printing (Rev B), doc 8e98ce79ede4, rendered
# at 300-600 dpi from the 400 dpi scan. The 1st printing (61ff2a1305d5) is the
# cross-check. tools/build_board_nets.py reads this file.
#
#   net NAME: PIN PIN ...   a net whose name is printed on the sheet
#   wire PIN PIN ...        an unnamed connection -- same net, no name on the sheet
#   sig PIN CODE [TEST]     a signature printed beside the pin (TEST defaults to 1)
#   nc PIN ...              a pin the sheet draws with nothing attached
#   label NAME: PIN ...     an unnamed net we have given a name to (not on the sheet)
#   value REF VALUE         a passive's value as printed
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. ICs are U + the grid position exactly as the sheet
# prints it (UC1, UH/J2), because the sheet also has a capacitor C1 and a
# resistor at R... -- the convention AGENTS.md sets for the KiCad projects. A
# spanning device keeps its span here (UH/J2); the build files it under its
# first cell (UH2), as the board map does. Passives are as printed (R1, C9).
#
# Connectors and test points are not designated on the sheet. These names are
# ours. The sheet's legend gives the symbols:
#   P1   game-PCB interconnect -- the legend's hexagon ("interconnect connector")
#   P2   edge connector -- the legend's square
#   SA   signature-analysis header -- circles, which the legend does not list;
#        the harness plugs on here (sheet 1 Side B's procedure)
#   TP1-TP5  the legend's pentagon flags ("test point"): +5V, GND, +22V, AUD+, AUD-
#
# Power pins of logic ICs are not drawn on this sheet except where noted; the
# build adds them from the part's standard pinout.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Math Box -- game-PCB interconnect P1
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
net E3MHZ: P1.1 UB4.2 UJ4.2 UD3.1 UD4.8
net E12KHZ: P1.2
net E6MHZ: P1.3 UB4.4
net GND: P1.4 P1.14 P1.16
net EPHI2: P1.12 UD4.2 UJ4.1 UE4.13
net /EI/O: P1.13 UC3.15
net ER/WB: P1.15 UC4.13 UE4.9 UD4.6
net EAB0: P1.11 UB1.10
net EAB1: P1.5 UB1.11
net EAB2: P1.10 UB1.12
net EAB3: P1.6 UB1.13 UC3.2
net EAB4: P1.9 UB1.14 UC3.3
net EAB5: P1.7 UC3.13
net EAB6: P1.8 UC3.14
net EDB0: P1.20 UF2.25 UF2.36 UD/E2.25 UD/E2.36
net EDB1: P1.21 UF2.24 UF2.37 UD/E2.24 UD/E2.37
net EDB2: P1.22 UF2.23 UF2.38 UD/E2.23 UD/E2.38
net EDB3: P1.23 UF2.22 UF2.39 UD/E2.22 UD/E2.39
net EDB4: P1.24 UK2.25 UK2.36 UH/J2.25 UH/J2.36
net EDB5: P1.19 UK2.24 UK2.37 UH/J2.24 UH/J2.37
net EDB6: P1.18 UK2.23 UK2.38 UH/J2.23 UH/J2.38
net EDB7: P1.17 UK2.22 UK2.39 UH/J2.22 UH/J2.39 UE3.3 R2.1
net +5V: R2.2 R1.2
value R1 470
value R2 1K

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Math Box -- start, stop and clock
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# B4 makes BEGIN: held clear while M START is low, then set on an E6MHZ edge
# with E3MHZ high, and toggled back off by its own /BEGIN on K.
net M START: UD4.1 UB4.1 SA.3
net BEGIN: UB4.6 UC1.1 UD5.2
net /BEGIN: UB4.7 UB4.3 UB1.15 UC5.13 UD5.13
wire UB4.5 R22.1
wire UC5.10 UC5.4 UC5.1 R22.1
wire UE1.7 UE1.1 UD1.1 R3.1
# R22 and R3 are pull-ups; the sheet prints "P,R22" and "P,R3" at each pin
net +5V: R22.2 R3.2
wire UC4.11 UD4.3 UE4.5
wire UE4.6 UJ4.5 UJ4.4
net SACLK3: UJ4.6 SA.8
wire UC3.9 UC4.12
# CLK runs while STOP is low: D4 NORs STOP with E3MHZ
net STOP: UC5.9 UD4.9 UE3.2 SA.4
net CLK: UD4.10 UE4.11 UD5.1 UC5.3 UE1.2 UD1.2 UK2.15 UF2.15 UH/J2.15 UD/E2.15 SA.6
net /CLK: UE4.10 UC5.11 UD5.9
net SACLK2: UD5.3 SA.7
nc UC5.8

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Math Box -- address decode and strobes to the rest of the board
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire UE4.12 UD4.5
wire UD4.4 UD3.2
wire UD3.3 UC4.10
wire UC3.10 UC4.9
net /OUTPUT LATCH: UC4.8
net /SWITCHES: UC3.11
wire UC3.12 UC4.5
wire UE4.8 UC4.4
wire UC4.6 UC3.1
net /YHI: UC3.7 UK2.40 UF2.40
net /YLO: UC3.6 UH/J2.40 UD/E2.40
nc UC3.5
wire UC3.4 UD4.11 UD4.12
wire UD4.13 UE3.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Math Box -- sequencer
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# B1 (entry PROM, addressed by EAB0-4) and C1 (jump-address latch) share one
# bus into the program counter E1/D1. B1 drives it while BEGIN, C1 otherwise.
wire UC1.19 UB1.1 UE1.3
wire UC1.2 UB1.2 UE1.4
wire UC1.16 UB1.3 UE1.5
wire UC1.5 UB1.4 UE1.6
wire UC1.15 UB1.5 UD1.3
wire UC1.6 UB1.6 UD1.4
wire UC1.12 UB1.7 UD1.5
wire UC1.9 UB1.9 UD1.6
wire UD5.8 UC1.11
# D5 pin 11: load the counter at BEGIN, or when the jump condition says so
wire UD5.11 UE1.10 UE1.9 UD1.10 UD1.9
wire UE1.15 UD1.7
nc UD1.15
# Microcode address bus: every PROM sees the same eight lines
label MA0: UE1.14 UM1.5 UL1.5 UK1.5 UJ1.5 UH1.5 UF1.5
label MA1: UE1.13 UM1.6 UL1.6 UK1.6 UJ1.6 UH1.6 UF1.6
label MA2: UE1.12 UM1.7 UL1.7 UK1.7 UJ1.7 UH1.7 UF1.7
label MA3: UE1.11 UM1.4 UL1.4 UK1.4 UJ1.4 UH1.4 UF1.4
label MA4: UD1.14 UM1.3 UL1.3 UK1.3 UJ1.3 UH1.3 UF1.3
label MA5: UD1.13 UM1.2 UL1.2 UK1.2 UJ1.2 UH1.2 UF1.2
label MA6: UD1.12 UM1.1 UL1.1 UK1.1 UJ1.1 UH1.1 UF1.1
label MA7: UD1.11 UM1.15 UL1.15 UK1.15 UJ1.15 UH1.15 UF1.15
net SAEN1: SA.9 UD1.11
# The six PROMs are always enabled
net GND: UM1.13 UM1.14 UL1.13 UL1.14 UK1.13 UK1.14 UJ1.13 UJ1.14 UH1.13 UH1.14 UF1.13 UF1.14

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Math Box -- microcode fields
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A0-A23 are the sheet's own names for the PROM outputs.
net A0: UM1.9 UC1.8 UK2.1 UF2.1 UH/J2.1 UD/E2.1
net A1: UM1.10 UC1.13 UK2.2 UF2.2 UH/J2.2 UD/E2.2
net A2: UM1.11 UC1.7 UK2.3 UF2.3 UH/J2.3 UD/E2.3
net A3: UM1.12 UC1.14 UK2.4 UF2.4 UH/J2.4 UD/E2.4
net A4: UL1.9 UC1.4 UK2.20 UF2.20 UH/J2.20 UD/E2.20
net A5: UL1.10 UC1.17 UK2.19 UF2.19 UH/J2.19 UD/E2.19
net A6: UL1.11 UC1.3 UK2.18 UF2.18 UH/J2.18 UD/E2.18
net A7: UL1.12 UC1.18 UK2.17 UF2.17 UH/J2.17 UD/E2.17
net A8: UK1.9 UK2.14 UF2.14
net A9: UK1.10 UH/J2.14 UD/E2.14
net A10: UK1.11 UE5.10
net A10*: UE5.8 UK2.13 UF2.13 UH/J2.13 UD/E2.13
net A11: UK1.12 UK2.12 UF2.12 UH/J2.12 UD/E2.12
net A12: UJ1.9 UC5.12
net A13: UJ1.10 UK2.27 UF2.27 UH/J2.27 UD/E2.27
net A14: UJ1.11 UK2.28 UF2.28 UH/J2.28 UD/E2.28
net A15: UJ1.12 UK2.26 UF2.26 UH/J2.26 UD/E2.26
net A16: UH1.9 UD5.10
net A17: UH1.10 UK2.6 UF2.6 UH/J2.6 UD/E2.6
net A18: UH1.11 UK2.7 UF2.7 UH/J2.7 UD/E2.7 UD3.4 UD3.5 UE3.9 UE3.10
net A19: UH1.12 UK2.5 UF2.5 UH/J2.5 UD/E2.5
net A20: UF1.9 UD3.12
net A21: UF1.10 UD3.9 SA.5
net A22: UF1.11 UD5.4
net A23: UF1.12 UD/E2.29

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Math Box -- the four Am2901 slices (Atari 137004-001)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# K2 is the most significant slice (its F3 and OVR are used), D/E2 the least.
# The sheet draws them left to right K2, F2, H/J2, D/E2. K2 and F2 put the high
# byte on EDB under /YHI; H/J2 and D/E2 the low byte under /YLO. Each slice's
# D inputs are tied to its own Y outputs (22-39, 23-38, 24-37, 25-36).
net +5V: UK2.10 UF2.10 UH/J2.10 UD/E2.10
net GND: UK2.30 UF2.30 UH/J2.30 UD/E2.30
# Carry and shift chains, less significant slice to more significant
wire UF2.33 UK2.29
wire UF2.8 UK2.9
wire UF2.16 UK2.21
wire UH/J2.33 UF2.29
wire UH/J2.8 UF2.9
wire UH/J2.16 UF2.21
wire UD/E2.33 UH/J2.29
wire UD/E2.8 UH/J2.9
wire UD/E2.16 UH/J2.21
# Double-length shift: the Q register's top bit into the RAM's bottom bit
wire UK2.16 UD/E2.9
# Sign logic: F3 XOR OVR, gated by A20, into the jump condition and RAM3 shift-in
wire UK2.31 UE5.12
wire UK2.34 UE5.13
wire UE5.11 UD3.13
wire UD3.11 UD3.10 UE3.13
wire UD3.6 UE3.12
wire UE3.11 R1.1 UK2.8
wire UD3.8 UD5.12
# /A18 (open collector) shifts a zero into Q0 of the least significant slice;
# C5 latches Q0 on each clock for the multiply step
wire UE3.8 UD/E2.21 UC5.2
wire UC5.6 UD5.5
wire UD5.6 UE5.9

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Math Box -- signatures printed on the sheet (Test #1 unless named)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
sig UM1.9 6CF6
sig UM1.10 F74F
sig UM1.11 1AA2
sig UM1.12 58A1
sig UL1.9 34C2
sig UL1.10 PPF6
sig UL1.11 60H6
sig UL1.12 05A6
sig UK1.9 3FU4
